            <h2 id="what-are-cookies">1. What are cookies?</h2>
            <p class="muted">Cookies are small text files placed on your device (computer, tablet, phone) by websites you visit. Cookies and similar technologies (including web beacons, pixels, local storage, and fingerprinting techniques) help websites function, remember choices, measure performance and deliver relevant content. Cookies may be set by JOOD (first-party) or by third parties (third-party cookies).</p>

            <h2 id="cookies-we-use">2. Cookies we use (detailed)</h2>
            <p class="muted">We categorise cookies by purpose. Below is a representative (non-exhaustive) list of cookie categories we use and examples of common cookies within each category.</p>

            <h3 class="category">Essential / Strictly necessary</h3>
            <p class="muted">These cookies are required for core site functionality (login, session management, shopping cart, security). They cannot be turned off in our systems.</p>
            <table class="table" aria-describedby="essential-cookies">
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Name / Example</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Typical retention</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>session_id</code></td><td>Session management and authenticated user state.</td><td>Session</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>cart_token</code></td><td>Preserve shopping cart contents between pages.</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <h3 class="category">Performance & Analytics</h3>
            <p class="muted">These cookies collect aggregated, anonymised information about how visitors use the site (pages visited, load times, errors) to help us improve performance and reliability.</p>
            <table class="table">
              <thead><tr><th>Name / Example</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Typical retention</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>_ga</code> (Google Analytics)</td><td>Distinct visitor identifier for analytics.</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>_gid</code></td><td>Used to distinguish users in analytics short-term.</td><td>24 hours</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <h3 class="category">Functional</h3>
            <p class="muted">Functional cookies remember user preferences and settings (language, region, accessibility preferences).</p>
            <table class="table">
              <thead><tr><th>Name / Example</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Typical retention</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>locale</code></td><td>Remember language and regional settings.</td><td>1 year</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>pref_theme</code></td><td>Store display preferences (e.g., compact view).</td><td>1 year</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <h3 class="category">Advertising & Marketing</h3>
            <p class="muted">These cookies are used to deliver relevant ads, measure campaign performance and limit ad repetition. They may be set by advertising networks and partners.</p>
            <table class="table">
              <thead><tr><th>Name / Example</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Typical retention</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>fr</code> (Facebook)</td><td>Ad targeting and measurement.</td><td>3 months</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>IDE</code> (DoubleClick)</td><td>Advertising targeting and frequency capping.</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <h2 id="legal-basis">3. Legal basis & consent</h2>
            <p class="muted">Where required by law (for example, under GDPR or UAE data protection requirements), we obtain your consent before placing non-essential cookies (analytics, advertising). Essential cookies that are strictly necessary to provide requested services do not require consent.</p>
            <p class="muted">When we ask for consent, we record the details (what you accepted, when, and from which IP/user-agent) for compliance and audit purposes. You can withdraw consent at any time — see <a href="#manage">Managing & Controlling Cookies</a> below.</p>

            <h2 id="how-long">4. Retention & lifetimes</h2>
            <p class="muted">Cookie lifetimes vary by type and provider. Session cookies expire when you close your browser. Persistent cookies remain until a set expiry date. We retain records of consent and cookie logs for compliance (typical retention: 2–7 years depending on legal and financial requirements).</p>

            <h2 id="third-parties">5. Third-party cookies & service providers</h2>
            <p class="muted">We may allow third-party providers to set cookies on our site for analytics, advertising, or service delivery (e.g., payment, chat, maps). These third parties have their own privacy policies and cookie controls. Examples include: Google Analytics, Google Ads / DoubleClick, Facebook/Meta, payment gateways, and CDN providers.</p>
            <p class="muted">We use contractual safeguards (Data Processing Agreements) to require partners to protect personal data in accordance with applicable law.</p>

            <h2 id="manage">6. Managing & controlling cookies</h2>
            <p class="muted">You can manage cookies using the tools below:</p>
            <ul class="muted value-list">
              <li><strong>Cookie banner / preference centre:</strong> Use our cookie banner (bottom of pages) to change category-level preferences and withdraw consent for non-essential cookies.</li>
              <li><strong>Browser controls:</strong> Most browsers allow you to block or delete cookies (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge). See your browser’s help pages for instructions.</li>
              <li><strong>Opt-out links:</strong> For advertising cookies you can opt out using industry opt-out tools (e.g., <a href="https://youradchoices.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YourAdChoices</a>, <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AboutAds</a>).</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">If you block or delete cookies, some parts of the Site may not function correctly (see <a href="#consequences">Consequences</a> below).</p>

            <h2 id="consequences">7. Consequences of blocking cookies</h2>
            <p class="muted">Blocking essential cookies may prevent you from logging in, using a shopping cart, or completing checkout. Blocking analytics/functional cookies may reduce site personalization and troubleshooting capabilities. Blocking advertising cookies will not stop ads entirely, but ads may be less relevant.</p>

            <h2 id="changes">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
            <p class="muted">We may update this Cookie Policy to reflect changes in technology, legal requirements, or business practices. Material changes will be communicated via the Site (notice banner) and to registered users where appropriate. Always check the effective date at the top of this page.</p>

            <h2 id="contact">9. Contact & complaints</h2>
            <p class="muted">If you have questions about our use of cookies, wish to withdraw consent, or want to make a privacy request, contact:</p>
            <p class="muted"><strong>Data Protection Officer (DPO)</strong><br>
              Email: <a href="mailto:dpo@jood.com">dpo@jood.com</a><br>
              Phone: +971-55-555-5555<br>
              Address: Al Reem Tower, Dubai, UAE</p>

            <p class="note" style="margin-top:12px;">This Cookie Policy should be read together with our <a href="/customer/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/customer/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

